{"id": 13535, "title": "Yǎn’ěr dào líng", "level": "Intermediate", "hsk_tags": ["HSK4"], "slug": "yaner-dao-ling", "audio_url": "/audio/mandarin/13535_yaner-dao-ling.mp3", "simplified_paragraphs": ["从前有一个人，看见别人家门口有一个大钟，就想把它偷走。可是钟又大又重，他就拿来一个铁锤，想把钟敲碎，然后一块一块地偷走。但是铁锤敲钟会有很大的声音，所有人都能听见，他肯定会被发现。他又想了想：如果敲钟的时候把自己的耳朵捂起来，就什么都听不到了！他觉得自己听不到声音，别人也一定听不到。然后他一边捂耳朵，一边用铁锤敲钟。很多人都听到了钟声，赶来把这个小偷抓住了。这个成语就是“掩耳盗铃”，我们经常用这个成语来比喻自己骗自己的行为。"], "traditional_paragraphs": ["從前有一個人，看見別人家門口有一個大鐘，就想把它偷走。可是鐘又大又重，他就拿來一個鐵錘，想把鐘敲碎，然後一塊一塊地偷走。但是鐵錘敲鐘會有很大的聲音，所有人都能聽見，他肯定會被發現。他又想了想：如果敲鐘的時候把自己的耳朵捂起來，就什麼都聽不到了！他覺得自己聽不到聲音，別人也一定聽不到。然後他一邊捂耳朵，一邊用鐵錘敲鐘。很多人都聽到了鐘聲，趕來把這個小偷抓住了。這個成語就是“掩耳盜鈴”，我們經常用這個成語來比喻自己騙自己的行為。"], "pinyin_paragraphs": ["cóng qián yǒu yī gè rén， kàn jiàn bié rén jiā mén kǒu yǒu yī gè dà zhōng， jiù xiǎng bǎ tā tōu zǒu。 kě shì zhōng yòu dà yòu zhòng， tā jiù ná lái yī gè tiě chuí， xiǎng bǎ zhōng qiāo suì， rán hòu yī kuài yī kuài de tōu zǒu。 dàn shì tiě chuí qiāo zhōng huì yǒu hěn dà de shēng yīn， suǒ yǒu rén dōu néng tīng jiàn， tā kěn dìng huì bèi fā xiàn。 tā yòu xiǎng le xiǎng： rú guǒ qiāo zhōng de shí hou bǎ zì jǐ de ěr duo wǔ qǐ lái， jiù shén me dōu tīng bù dào le！ tā jué de zì jǐ tīng bù dào shēng yīn， bié rén yě yī dìng tīng bù dào。 rán hòu tā yī biān wǔ ěr duo， yī biān yòng tiě chuí qiāo zhōng。 hěn duō rén dōu tīng dào le zhōng shēng， gǎn lái bǎ zhè gè xiǎo tōu zhuā zhù le。 zhè gè chéng yǔ jiù shì“ yǎn ěr dào líng”， wǒ men jīng cháng yòng zhè gè chéng yǔ lái bǐ yù zì jǐ piàn zì jǐ de xíng wéi。"], "english_paragraphs": ["Once upon a time, there was a man who saw a big clock at the door of someone else's house and wanted to steal it. But the bell was big and heavy, so he took a hammer and tried to break it into pieces, then steal it piece by piece. But the hammer striking the bell will make a loud sound that can be heard by everyone, and he will definitely be discovered. He thought again: If he covered his ears when ringing the bell, he would hear nothing! He felt that if he couldn't hear the sound, others wouldn't be able to hear it either. Then he struck the bell with a hammer while covering his ears. Many people heard the bell and came to catch the thief. This idiom is \"hiding one's ears and stealing the bell\". We often use this idiom to describe our behavior of deceiving ourselves."], "english_full": "Once upon a time, there was a man who saw a big clock at the door of someone else's house and wanted to steal it. But the bell was big and heavy, so he took a hammer and tried to break it into pieces, then steal it piece by piece. But the hammer striking the bell will make a loud sound that can be heard by everyone, and he will definitely be discovered. He thought again: If he covered his ears when ringing the bell, he would hear nothing! He felt that if he couldn't hear the sound, others wouldn't be able to hear it either. Then he struck the bell with a hammer while covering his ears. Many people heard the bell and came to catch the thief. This idiom is \"hiding one's ears and stealing the bell\". We often use this idiom to describe our behavior of deceiving ourselves.", "ruby_paragraphs": ["<ruby class=\"mb-tooltip\" data-py=\"cóng qián\" data-defn=\"previously / formerly / once upon a time\" data-hsk=\"HSK 5\"><span class=\"si\">从前</span><span class=\"tr\">從前</span><rt>cóng qián</rt></ruby><ruby class=\"mb-tooltip\" data-py=\"yǒu\" data-defn=\"to have; there is\" data-hsk=\"HSK 1\"><span class=\"si\">有</span><span class=\"tr\">有</span><rt>yǒu</rt></ruby><ruby class=\"mb-tooltip\" data-py=\"yī\" data-defn=\"one / single / a (article)\" data-hsk=\"HSK 1\"><span class=\"si\">一</span><span class=\"tr\">一</span><rt>yī</rt></ruby><ruby class=\"mb-tooltip\" data-py=\"gè\" data-defn=\"classifier for people or objects in general\" data-hsk=\"HSK 1\"><span class=\"si\">个</span><span class=\"tr\">個</span><rt>gè</rt></ruby><ruby class=\"mb-tooltip\" data-py=\"rén\" data-defn=\"person; people\" data-hsk=\"HSK 1\"><span class=\"si\">人</span><span class=\"tr\">人</span><rt>rén</r